{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "את הכבש האחד", :translit "et ha-keves ha-echad", :gloss "the one lamb"} {:he "אחד", :translit "echad", :gloss "one"} {:he "האחד", :translit "ha-echad", :gloss "the one"} {:he "אחד", :translit "echad", :gloss "one"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "האחד", :b "י\"ח"} {:kind :masorah, :count 1, :occurrences ["אחד"]}], :frame {:text "The eighteen blessings of the Amidah prayer were instituted corresponding to the daily offerings; this count is traced back to the eighteen times the word 'blessing' appears near the patriarchs, or eighteen references to the daily offering in its passage (Berakhot 28b, Yoma 70b, Megillah 17b–18a). Pinchas is the locus of this correspondence because the daily offering is mandated in Numbers 28 (cf. Berakhot 26b). The priests' occupation with the daily offering is detailed in Tractate Yoma (Yoma 28a, 31a–33a).", :sources ["Berakhot 26b" "Berakhot 28b" "Yoma 28a" "Yoma 31a" "Yoma 33a" "Yoma 70b" "Megillah 17b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "את הכבש האחד תעשה בבוקר", :translit "et ha-keves ha-echad ta'aseh va-boker", :gloss "the one lamb you shall prepare in the morning"} {:he "תעשה", :translit "ta'aseh", :gloss "you shall prepare"} {:he "תשעה", :translit "tish'ah", :gloss "nine"} {:he "ואת השני בערב", :translit "ve-et ha-sheini ba-erev", :gloss "and the second in the evening"} {:he "תעשה", :translit "ta'aseh", :gloss "you shall prepare"} {:he "תעשו", :translit "ta'asu", :gloss "you shall prepare"} {:he "תמידין", :translit "tamidin", :gloss "daily offerings"} {:he "כבשים הכבש הכבש לכבש הכבש", :translit "kvasim ha-keves ha-keves la-keves ha-keves", :gloss "lambs the lamb the lamb for the lamb the lamb"} {:he "עולה", :translit "olah", :gloss "burnt offering"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "תעשה", :b "תשעה"} {:kind :masorah, :count 6, :occurrences ["כבשים" "הכבש" "הכבש" "לכבש" "הכבש"]} {:kind :masorah, :count 6, :occurrences ["עולה"]} {:kind :other, :note "Singular תעשה vs plural תעשו teaches individual may donate daily offerings to the public."}], :frame {:text "Nine priests performed the morning daily offering: two held the two forelegs, two the hind legs, one the head, one the right flank, one the neck, and two the intestines (Yoma 26a). The evening offering required two additional priests to carry the two pieces of wood for the altar fire (Yoma 26a, Tamid 31b). The Chamber of Lambs where the inspected animals were kept is described in the Mishnah (Middot 1:6, Tamid 3:4, Shekalim 5:4–6). The portion of the Akedah is Genesis 22, where עולה appears (Genesis 22:2–8).", :sources ["Yoma 26a" "Tamid 31b" "Middot 1:6" "Tamid 3:4" "Shekalim 5:4" "Shekalim 5:5" "Shekalim 5:6" "Genesis 22:2" "Genesis 22:3" "Genesis 22:8"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "האחד", :a-value 18, :b "י\"ח", :b-value 18, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :masorah, :count 1, :occurrences ["אחד"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "אחד", :refs ["Genesis 1:5" "Genesis 1:9" "Genesis 2:24" "Genesis 11:6" "Genesis 21:15" "Genesis 22:2" "Genesis 26:10" "Genesis 27:45"], :n 400, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :gematria, :a "תעשה", :a-value 775, :b "תשעה", :b-value 775, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :masorah, :count 6, :occurrences ["כבשים" "הכבש" "הכבש" "לכבש" "הכבש"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "כבשים", :refs ["Exodus 29:38" "Leviticus 14:10" "Leviticus 23:18" "Leviticus 23:19" "Leviticus 23:20" "Numbers 7:17" "Numbers 7:23" "Numbers 7:29"], :n 43, :lens :exact} {:phrase "הכבש", :refs ["Exodus 29:39" "Exodus 29:41" "Leviticus 14:12" "Leviticus 14:13" "Numbers 28:4" "Numbers 28:8" "Ezekiel 46:15"], :n 7, :lens :exact} {:phrase "הכבש", :refs ["Exodus 29:39" "Exodus 29:41" "Leviticus 14:12" "Leviticus 14:13" "Numbers 28:4" "Numbers 28:8" "Ezekiel 46:15"], :n 7, :lens :exact} {:phrase "לכבש", :refs ["Exodus 29:40" "Numbers 15:5" "Numbers 28:7" "Numbers 28:13" "Numbers 28:14" "Numbers 28:21" "Numbers 28:29" "Numbers 29:4"], :n 11, :lens :exact} {:phrase "הכבש", :r